#################################################################
#  ENRICHED DETAIL FOR KEY SECTIONS (deeply extracted from source)
#################################################################

gst:CGST_Section2 rdfs:comment "Sec 2 defines ~120 terms used throughout the CGST Act, including 'aggregate turnover' (2(6)), 'business' (2(17)), 'casual taxable person' (2(20)), 'composite supply' (2(30)), 'electronic commerce operator' (2(45)), 'exempt supply' (2(47)), 'input tax credit' (2(63)), 'mixed supply' (2(74)), 'non-taxable supply' (2(78)), 'person' (2(84)), 'proper officer' (2(91)), 'registered person' (2(94)), 'taxable person' (2(107)), 'taxable supply' (2(108))."@en .

gst:CGST_Section7 rdfs:comment "Defines the scope of 'supply': all forms of supply of goods/services for consideration in the course/furtherance of business (incl. transactions with members per clause (aa) inserted retrospectively from 01.07.2017), import of services for consideration, and Schedule I activities without consideration; excludes Schedule III activities and notified government activities."@en .

gst:CGST_Section9 rdfs:comment "Sec 9(1): CGST levied on intra-State supplies at a rate notified by Government (max 20%) on the recommendations of the GST Council, payable by the supplier (subject to Sec 9(4) - petroleum products currently outside GST for this sub-section). Sec 9(3)/(4): reverse charge on notified supplies / supplies from unregistered persons."@en .

gst:CGST_Section10 rdfs:comment "Composition levy: Sec 10(1) - manufacturers/other suppliers of goods (and Schedule II para 6(b) restaurant-type services) with preceding-FY aggregate turnover not exceeding the notified limit (Rs 50 lakh, enhanceable up to Rs 1.5 crore, Rs 75 lakh for specified special category States) may opt to pay 1% / 2.5%+2.5% / 0.5%+0.5% of turnover in lieu of normal tax, subject to conditions in the proviso (no inter-State outward supply, no supply through e-commerce collecting TCS except as permitted, no supply of non-permitted services beyond the higher of 10% of turnover or Rs 5 lakh, etc.). Sec 10(2A) extends a parallel composition option (rate up to 3%+3%) to service providers with turnover up to Rs 50 lakh."@en .

gst:CGST_Section16 rdfs:comment "ITC eligibility conditions (Sec 16(2)): possession of tax invoice/debit note, communication of invoice details under Sec 37 (not restricted under Sec 38), receipt of goods/services, tax actually paid to Government by supplier, and furnishing of return under Sec 39. Payment to supplier required within 180 days (else ITC to be reversed with interest). Sec 16(4): ITC cannot be claimed after 30 November following the end of the relevant financial year (or date of furnishing the annual return, if earlier)."@en .

gst:CGST_Section17 rdfs:comment "Sec 17(1)/(2): apportionment of credit where goods/services are used partly for business and partly for other purposes, or partly for taxable/zero-rated and partly for exempt supplies - credit restricted to the business/taxable portion. Sec 17(5): blocked credits list (motor vehicles/conveyances subject to exceptions, food & beverages, outdoor catering, health/fitness/club membership, works contract services for immovable property other than plant & machinery, goods/services for construction of immovable property on own account, tax paid under composition levy, goods/services for personal consumption, goods lost/stolen/destroyed/written off or disposed of as gifts/free samples, and tax paid under demand for fraud/suppression cases)."@en .

gst:CGST_Section22 rdfs:comment "Every supplier is liable to register in the State/UT from where a taxable supply is made if aggregate turnover in a financial year exceeds Rs 20 lakh (Rs 10 lakh for special category States); the Government may, by notification, raise this general limit up to Rs 40 lakh for a supplier engaged EXCLUSIVELY in the supply of goods (subject to conditions)."@en ;
    gst:hasThreshold gst:ThresholdRegistrationGeneral20L, gst:ThresholdRegistrationSpecialCategory10L, gst:ThresholdRegistrationGoodsOnly40L .

gst:CGST_Section23 rdfs:comment "Persons not liable for registration: (a) persons exclusively engaged in supplying wholly-exempt or non-taxable goods/services; (b) agriculturists, to the extent of supply of produce out of cultivation of land; and (c) such other persons/categories as the Government may notify on Council recommendation."@en .

gst:CGST_Section24 rdfs:comment "Compulsory registration irrespective of turnover for 11 categories, including: inter-State suppliers; casual taxable persons; persons liable under reverse charge; persons liable to pay tax under Sec 9(5) (electronic commerce); non-resident taxable persons; persons required to deduct TDS; agents supplying on behalf of others; Input Service Distributors; persons supplying through an e-commerce operator (subject to notified exceptions); every electronic commerce operator required to collect TCS; and other notified categories."@en .

gst:CGST_Section39 rdfs:comment "Prescribes the returns to be furnished by different categories of registered persons (normal taxpayers under Sec 39(1)/monthly-or-QRMP, composition taxpayers under Sec 39(2)/quarterly, non-resident taxable persons, ISDs, and TDS deductors) and their respective due dates."@en .

gst:CGST_Section44 rdfs:comment "Every registered person (other than an ISD, a casual/non-resident taxable person, and a person paying tax under Sec 51/52) must furnish an annual return, which may include a self-certified reconciliation statement, for every financial year, by the notified due date."@en .

gst:CGST_Section50 rdfs:comment "Sec 50(1): interest at 18% p.a. on tax paid after the due date (computed, post-amendment, only on the portion of liability discharged by debiting the electronic cash ledger). Sec 50(3): interest at 24% p.a. where ITC has been wrongly availed AND utilised."@en ;
    gst:hasThreshold gst:ThresholdInterestDelayedPayment18Pct, gst:ThresholdInterestWrongITC24Pct .

gst:CGST_Section51 rdfs:comment "Specified deductors (Government departments/agencies, local authorities, PSUs, and notified persons) must deduct TDS at 1% CGST + 1% SGST (or 2% IGST) from payments to a supplier under a contract of taxable supply where the total contract value exceeds Rs 2,50,000 (excluding tax)."@en ;
    gst:hasThreshold gst:ThresholdTDSContractValue250K ;
    gst:hasApplicableSection gst:CGST_Section51 .

gst:CGST_Section52 rdfs:comment "Every e-commerce operator (other than an agent) must collect TCS not exceeding 1% (notified at 0.5% CGST + 0.5% SGST, or 1% IGST) of the net value of taxable supplies made through it by other suppliers where the operator collects the consideration."@en .

gst:CGST_Section54 rdfs:comment "Refund claims must be made within 2 years of the relevant date. Documentary evidence of no unjust enrichment is waived (self-declaration suffices) for claims not exceeding Rs 2 lakh. Up to 90% of a zero-rated-supply refund claim may be granted provisionally within 60 days of acknowledgment of the complete application, subject to conditions; balance sanctioned after verification."@en ;
    gst:hasThreshold gst:ThresholdRefundLimitationPeriod2Yr, gst:ThresholdRefundDocEvidenceWaiver2L .

gst:CGST_Section65 rdfs:comment "Commissioner (or an authorised officer) may undertake audit of a registered person's records at the place of business or in office, with at least 15 working days' prior notice; to be completed within 3 months, extendable by the Commissioner by a further 6 months for reasons recorded in writing."@en .

gst:CGST_Section66 rdfs:comment "Special audit may be directed, with the Commissioner's prior approval, by an officer not below the rank of Assistant Commissioner, having regard to the nature and complexity of the case and the interest of revenue, to be conducted by a nominated Chartered Accountant or Cost Accountant, normally within 90 days (extendable by 90 days)."@en .

gst:CGST_Section107 rdfs:comment "Appeal to the Appellate Authority within 3 months of communication of the order (condonable by a further 1 month for sufficient cause). Pre-deposit: the full amount of admitted tax/interest/fine/fee/penalty, PLUS 10% of the remaining disputed tax amount, subject to a cap of Rs 20 crore."@en ;
    gst:hasThreshold gst:ThresholdAppealLimitation3Months, gst:ThresholdAppealPreDeposit10Pct, gst:ThresholdAppealPreDepositCap20Cr .

gst:CGST_Section122 rdfs:comment "Sec 122(1) lists 21 specified offences (supply without invoice, invoice without supply, tax collected but not remitted beyond 3 months, fraudulent ITC availment/distribution, failure to register, obstruction of officers, tampering with evidence, etc.), each attracting a penalty of Rs 10,000 or the tax evaded/ITC wrongly availed/distributed (whichever is higher). Sec 122(2): general penalty for short-payment/non-payment of tax - the higher of Rs 10,000 or 10% of the tax due (non-fraud), or the higher of Rs 10,000 or the tax evaded (fraud)."@en .

gst:IGST_Section16 rdfs:comment "Zero rated supply = export of goods/services, or supply to a SEZ developer/unit. A registered person may supply under bond/LUT without payment of IGST and claim refund of unutilised ITC, or pay IGST and claim refund of the tax paid (subject to restrictions notified by Government on specified goods/services/persons, and subject to Sec 54 CGST Act refund conditions)."@en .

#################################################################
#  INDIVIDUALS: THRESHOLDS
#################################################################

gst:ThresholdRegistrationGeneral20L a owl:NamedIndividual, gst:Threshold ;
    gst:thresholdAmount "2000000"^^xsd:decimal ; gst:thresholdCurrency "INR" ;
    gst:legalCitation "Sec 22(1) first proviso omitted / main provision, CGST Act 2017" ;
    rdfs:label "Registration Threshold - General (Rs 20 Lakh)"@en .
gst:ThresholdRegistrationSpecialCategory10L a owl:NamedIndividual, gst:Threshold ;
    gst:thresholdAmount "1000000"^^xsd:decimal ; gst:thresholdCurrency "INR" ;
    gst:legalCitation "Sec 22(1) proviso, CGST Act 2017" ;
    rdfs:label "Registration Threshold - Special Category States (Rs 10 Lakh)"@en .
gst:ThresholdRegistrationGoodsOnly40L a owl:NamedIndividual, gst:Threshold ;
    gst:thresholdAmount "4000000"^^xsd:decimal ; gst:thresholdCurrency "INR" ;
    gst:legalCitation "Sec 22(1) proviso (notified enhancement), CGST Act 2017; Notification 10/2019-CT" ;
    rdfs:label "Registration Threshold - Goods-Only Supplier, Notified States (Rs 40 Lakh)"@en ;
    gst:sourceNote "Enhancement is optional per State; not all States adopted the Rs 40 lakh limit for goods suppliers." .
gst:ThresholdCompositionGoods1_5Cr a owl:NamedIndividual, gst:Threshold ;
    gst:thresholdAmount "15000000"^^xsd:decimal ; gst:thresholdCurrency "INR" ;
    gst:legalCitation "Sec 10(1) proviso, CGST Act 2017" ;
    rdfs:label "Composition Threshold - Goods, General States (Rs 1.5 Crore)"@en .
gst:ThresholdCompositionGoodsSpecialCategory75L a owl:NamedIndividual, gst:Threshold ;
    gst:thresholdAmount "7500000"^^xsd:decimal ; gst:thresholdCurrency "INR" ;
    gst:legalCitation "Sec 10(1) proviso, CGST Act 2017 (specified special category States)" ;
    rdfs:label "Composition Threshold - Goods, Specified Special Category States (Rs 75 Lakh)"@en ;
    gst:sourceNote "The source manual's Sec 10 text confirms a lower enhanced ceiling applies for specified special category States without itemising which of the four (Manipur, Mizoram, Nagaland, Tripura) adopted Rs 75 lakh vs a different figure; modelled here as the commonly-notified Rs 75 lakh figure pending State-wise confirmation." .
gst:ThresholdCompositionServices50L a owl:NamedIndividual, gst:Threshold ;
    gst:thresholdAmount "5000000"^^xsd:decimal ; gst:thresholdCurrency "INR" ;
    gst:legalCitation "Sec 10(2A), CGST Act 2017" ;
    rdfs:label "Composition Threshold - Services under Sec 10(2A) (Rs 50 Lakh)"@en .
gst:ThresholdInterestDelayedPayment18Pct a owl:NamedIndividual, gst:Threshold ;
    gst:thresholdAmount "18"^^xsd:decimal ; gst:thresholdCurrency "PERCENT" ;
    gst:legalCitation "Sec 50(1), CGST Act 2017" ;
    rdfs:label "Interest Rate - Delayed Payment (18% p.a.)"@en .
gst:ThresholdInterestWrongITC24Pct a owl:NamedIndividual, gst:Threshold ;
    gst:thresholdAmount "24"^^xsd:decimal ; gst:thresholdCurrency "PERCENT" ;
    gst:legalCitation "Sec 50(3), CGST Act 2017" ;
    rdfs:label "Interest Rate - Wrongly Availed & Utilised ITC (24% p.a.)"@en .
gst:ThresholdTDSContractValue250K a owl:NamedIndividual, gst:Threshold ;
    gst:thresholdAmount "250000"^^xsd:decimal ; gst:thresholdCurrency "INR" ;
    gst:legalCitation "Sec 51(1), CGST Act 2017" ;
    rdfs:label "TDS Applicability Threshold - Contract Value (Rs 2,50,000)"@en .
gst:ThresholdTDSRate1Pct a owl:NamedIndividual, gst:Threshold ;
    gst:thresholdAmount "1"^^xsd:decimal ; gst:thresholdCurrency "PERCENT" ;
    gst:legalCitation "Sec 51(1), CGST Act 2017" ; rdfs:label "TDS Rate (1% CGST + 1% SGST)"@en .
gst:ThresholdTCSRate1Pct a owl:NamedIndividual, gst:Threshold ;
    gst:thresholdAmount "1"^^xsd:decimal ; gst:thresholdCurrency "PERCENT" ;
    gst:legalCitation "Sec 52(1), CGST Act 2017; Notification 52/2018-CT" ; rdfs:label "TCS Rate (up to 1%, notified 0.5%+0.5%)"@en .
gst:ThresholdRefundLimitationPeriod2Yr a owl:NamedIndividual, gst:Threshold ;
    gst:thresholdAmount "2"^^xsd:decimal ; gst:thresholdCurrency "YEARS" ;
    gst:legalCitation "Sec 54(1), CGST Act 2017" ; rdfs:label "Refund Claim Limitation Period (2 Years)"@en .
gst:ThresholdRefundDocEvidenceWaiver2L a owl:NamedIndividual, gst:Threshold ;
    gst:thresholdAmount "200000"^^xsd:decimal ; gst:thresholdCurrency "INR" ;
    gst:legalCitation "Sec 54(4) proviso, CGST Act 2017" ; rdfs:label "Refund Documentary-Evidence Waiver Threshold (Rs 2 Lakh)"@en .
gst:ThresholdRefundProvisional90Pct a owl:NamedIndividual, gst:Threshold ;
    gst:thresholdAmount "90"^^xsd:decimal ; gst:thresholdCurrency "PERCENT" ;
    gst:legalCitation "Sec 54(6), CGST Act 2017" ; rdfs:label "Provisional Refund Percentage (90%)"@en .
gst:ThresholdEInvoicing5Cr a owl:NamedIndividual, gst:Threshold ;
    gst:thresholdAmount "50000000"^^xsd:decimal ; gst:thresholdCurrency "INR" ;
    gst:legalCitation "Rule 48(4), CGST Rules 2017; Notification 10/2023-CT dt. 10.05.2023" ;
    rdfs:label "E-Invoicing Applicability Threshold (Rs 5 Crore, w.e.f. 01.08.2023)"@en ;
    gst:sourceNote "E-invoicing threshold has been progressively lowered by successive notifications: Rs 500 Cr (2020) -> Rs 100 Cr -> Rs 50 Cr -> Rs 20 Cr -> Rs 10 Cr -> Rs 5 Cr (current, from 01.08.2023)." .
gst:ThresholdEWayBill50K a owl:NamedIndividual, gst:Threshold ;
    gst:thresholdAmount "50000"^^xsd:decimal ; gst:thresholdCurrency "INR" ;
    gst:legalCitation "Rule 138(1), CGST Rules 2017" ;
    rdfs:label "E-Way Bill Applicability Threshold - Consignment Value (Rs 50,000)"@en .
gst:ThresholdAppealLimitation3Months a owl:NamedIndividual, gst:Threshold ;
    gst:thresholdAmount "3"^^xsd:decimal ; gst:thresholdCurrency "MONTHS" ;
    gst:legalCitation "Sec 107(1), CGST Act 2017" ; rdfs:label "Appeal Limitation Period (3 Months, +1 month condonable)"@en .
gst:ThresholdAppealPreDeposit10Pct a owl:NamedIndividual, gst:Threshold ;
    gst:thresholdAmount "10"^^xsd:decimal ; gst:thresholdCurrency "PERCENT" ;
    gst:legalCitation "Sec 107(6), CGST Act 2017" ; rdfs:label "Appeal Pre-Deposit Percentage (10% of Disputed Tax)"@en .
gst:ThresholdAppealPreDepositCap20Cr a owl:NamedIndividual, gst:Threshold ;
    gst:thresholdAmount "200000000"^^xsd:decimal ; gst:thresholdCurrency "INR" ;
    gst:legalCitation "Sec 107(6), CGST Act 2017" ; rdfs:label "Appeal Pre-Deposit Cap (Rs 20 Crore)"@en .
gst:ThresholdForwardChargeRateCap20Pct a owl:NamedIndividual, gst:Threshold ;
    gst:thresholdAmount "20"^^xsd:decimal ; gst:thresholdCurrency "PERCENT" ;
    gst:legalCitation "Sec 9(1), CGST Act 2017" ;
    rdfs:label "Statutory Cap on CGST Rate (20%, mirrored by SGST/UTGST -> effective 40% combined cap)"@en .

